    "done_when": "Continue from 79c98c14f (failed run r-20261003T141823788120; its report /home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/reports/nova/s22/cco-certificate-ladder-110-300.md shows every exact row equal to its whole-cell control to the digit because clip_mode was not passed in the typed request). The driver under docs/figures/centroid-constrained-oracle-solve/certificate-ladder-110-300/ passes the support mode explicitly in every typed solve request (exact for the certificate rows, the whole-cell mode for the controls), and refuses to write a row receipt when the realised operator support mode differs from the requested one or when an exact row and its control share a terminal state digest. The control uses the exact arm derived centroid tolerance. Each row receipt records the accepted Newton promotions and, when there are none, the solver history field that says why. ONE H200 job (betelgeuse, gpu_0003_grpA, one card, 8 CPUs, --mem=128G, --time=02:00:00, TMPDIR=/tmp in submit and payload, the shared interpreter /home/ITER/mcintos/Code/nova/.venv/bin/python without uv, RECKON_ALLOW_NESTED_LAUNCH=1 sbatch; if still PENDING on resources after a minute, titan) runs weak, moderate and strong at -110 and -300 cells, both arms, from the production seed, each row persisted as it lands; once the job is admitted, commit, write status waiting with the sacct probe and job id, and end the turn. The resumed turn re-renders the twelve line-contour panels (shared levels, both null sets, wall, residual and converged flag in the caption), rewrites the report table with the clause verdicts, the accepted-promotion count per row and whether exact and control differ, and updates the fragment. A row that fails a clause is reported as measured, never tuned; no source under nova/ is edited. Keep scratch under the run directory.",
